  // ==========================================================================
  // Wave 7 (paideia-os #2446) -- UDP send/recv path (sysnos 96..97)
  // Both are 5-arg: SysV rdi/rsi/rdx/rcx/r8 -> SYSCALL rdi/rsi/rdx/r10/r9.
  // TWO-move shuffle (`mov r10, rcx; mov r9, r8`) mirrors sys_mount:
  // entry.pdx's SYSCALL-ABI -> SysV-C shuffle (`mov r8, r10`) clobbers
  // raw r8 without reading it, so a 5th arg staged in the SysV r8 slot
  // is destroyed; r9 is the one register entry.pdx never touches and
  // rides through into dispatch's r9 slot -- the only viable arg4 home.
  // See sys_mount's own header (this same file) for the full wire trace.
  // ==========================================================================

  // sys_sendto(fd, buf, len, dst_ip, dst_port) -> bytes sent or negative errno.
